Z||000000||b lo 0||03-21-2001||09:43 AM||||Alright, after a new fuel pump and spark plugs, NOTHING is better, and in fact, the GT is sitting immobilized at school due to the fact that the fuel pump will not work half the time.  I am almost POSITIVE it is the fuel pressure sensor.  The rev limiting is still there, although it revs smoother with the new plugs.  Old plugs were gapped right, but the wrong plugs.  Please let me know about your opinions.  Thnx guys and gals!<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">     <BR>Go to <A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.i-p.com" TARGET=_blank>www.audioimagery.i-p.com</A>  !!!<P><A HREF="http://clubs.excite.com/welcome/main?cid=.zXb1DJ1lsCL&aid=22&auth=" TARGET=_blank>Pontiac Fiero Owner's Club</A>-Pics, Videos and More-Or Post your Own||||reg||1
